    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "PKWWy",
      "x": -480,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Log · Cockpit",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-surface",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-card",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-3",
      "padding": 20,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "NexCB",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Log · Cockpit",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "lGDPw",
          "name": "2026-09-17 D126 D127",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-17 · D126 · Análisis' indicators card draws its chip for a reading from today, \"Lectura de las 11:30\". D127 · every signal row on Panorama, Panorama desktop and Señales carries Tendencia or Rebote under its verb; the arrows already drew the move for every sample. MovementItem's Tag is replaced per instance by a Verbo column — the kit gap is logged in ui-kit.CHANGELOG.md",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "QMwNv",
          "name": "2026-09-17",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-17 · D123 · Estados financieros' source label reads Yahoo Finance, which has written every statement since D109. D124's line items are not drawn here — the card draws its tabs and label only",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ayP03",
          "name": "Log 2026-09-16 D78",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-16 · Through CHECKLIST.md under D78. Kit 1.0.0 vendored and HeaderBar added; TopBarDetail deleted with no consumers. Panorama, Señales and Consolidado mirrored to the code; the asset detail redrawn from its partials — Mi posición's invented set, the RSI mini scale and the portfolio share retired. Asset · Análisis · Desktop v1 retired: the page reflows. Drawn: Panorama · Primera vez, Señales · Vacío, Consolidado · Sin historial, Asset · CETES. Code side: Panorama lit on Señales, the signals subtitle states its window, the empty radar stops asking a holder for a first trade, the detail's tabs light and its page is titled with the symbol, and the crypto card stops pointing at a retired tab",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "T7YWl",
          "name": "Log 2026-09-11 retire v1",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-11 · Asset · Análisis / v1 · deprecated is retired. It was kept for the side-by-side until v2 shipped; v2 shipped, so keeping it is keeping a second answer to the same question. Git holds it · D114",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "g3NOKQ",
          "name": "Log 2026-09-11 D114 copies",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-11 · The other two charts catch up to the 240 plot: the TradingView notice and the desktop detail carried their own baked copies of the 167 pane, so D103's 'three copies that agree today, with nothing keeping them in step' had come true. Same transform, applied by node name rather than by id, validated before writing. The notice drops its v1 marker — the chart card and the sheet are all it draws; the desktop keeps it, its three-card body still owes the fusion · D114, D103",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "t8mRt",
          "name": "Log 2026-09-11 D114",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-11 · The price pane grows 167 → 240, D114's fifth and last move. The three series are re-baked by scaling every relative dy by 240/167, the grid, level and cost lines by the same factor, and their labels and badges re-placed at their own 7px and 9px offsets rather than scaled; the declared transform moves with them, so the chart stays checkable. The RSI pane keeps its 64. CHART_HEIGHT 260 → 333 · D114, D103",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "D0cfe",
          "name": "Log 2026-09-11 D115",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-11 · Fundamentales: the line under each extract value now reads that value in words instead of naming what the metric measures — the description moves behind the ⓘ, where it already sat, and the growth line stops claiming a quarter-on-quarter change the figure never was. Deuda / Capital drawn with its real 0.15, which D116's fix put back on screen · D115",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "kQ4Vk",
          "name": "Entries",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-06 · Asset · Análisis / Propuesta drawn from a copy of the real artboard: Señales, Niveles and Observaciones fused into one card, the moving averages lifted above the RSI, the verdict rewritten against the measurement, the fill rate added as a constant. The plot's height is NOT drawn — the price and bands are baked paths and stretching the frame would break D103 · D113, D114, D115\n2026-09-06 · The O/H/L/C strip follows the crosshair and falls back to the latest bar; Vol prints — over the permanent hole in the stored history. Touch needed no branch — the library holds the crosshair after the finger lifts · D112\n2026-09-06 · Fundamentales becomes rows in one card rather than a grid of cards inside a card — the shape the artboard always drew, and the brief's open finding on it closes here · D111\n2026-09-06 · The RSI pane gains a visible separator and margin against it: it had its name and its scale but nothing said it was a second pane · D108\n2026-09-06 · Señales rows carry a directional accent and their figures name themselves; ATR joins the card without a chip · D110\n2026-09-06 · The three financial statements move to yfinance with Alpha Vantage as fallback — Alpha Vantage's free tier refuses BALANCE_SHEET, which had left the whole health category empty · D109",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "QxSM0",
          "name": "Entries",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-06 · The chart stops being a drawing. Its every value now comes from NVDA's real production series through the app's own indicators, and the price→y transform is a declared variable set measured from the shipping chart · D103\n2026-09-06 · Five defects the first real series exposed, fixed in code rather than in the canvas: the time axis was en-US, tu costo rendered no label, the RSI pane was unnamed and autoscaled, the level badges covered the recent 40% of the plot, and the cost line landed off-scale on short ranges · D104, D105, D106, D107, D108\n2026-09-06 · Brief consolidated — dates moved here, reasoning left to its D number, the duplicated O/H/L/C and Rendimiento rules merged, and §4 grouped by surface",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "x0uZ5",
          "name": "Entries",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-06 · The canvas catches up to the chart that shipped — levels named, priced and coloured by kind; the O/H/L/C strip moved up beside the range control and dropped its currency prefix; the legend's checkbox count made conditional on the range · D101, D102",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "yKX6B",
          "name": "Entries",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-06 · Rendimiento loses its Equity sparkline — retired, not deferred (#615, D97). The share figure stays drawn and still owes its own verdict",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Co3N5",
          "name": "Entries",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-06 · Capas — the chart's three overlays go behind a legend, all on by default; the range pills lead the card; tu costo gains a tick on the 52-week bar and loses its semantic colour; the Niveles card lands on both artboards. The old Default artboards are retired and these take their names · D96",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "A0vHIs",
          "name": "Entries",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-05 · #611 · Rendimiento is BUILT; the artboard's four windows became five and its percentages became money · D95\n2026-09-05 · CKP-2 · the chart's range control and O/H/L/C/Vol strip are BUILT; the artboard drew both and the code had neither · D93\n2026-09-05 · #607 · the TradingView toggle and its notice are BUILT; the CSP claim D66 carried was wrong and is corrected — the iframe is served from tradingview-widget.com, not *.tradingview.com\n2026-09-05 · kit 0.8.1 · TradingView opt-in toggle drawn at the foot of Chart (mobile + desktop) and the one-time notice added as Aviso TradingView; band reflowed · D66 · #606\n2026-09-05 · D88 · Cerrar posición is BUILT as a shortcut into the sell sheet — the artboard drew it and the tab had no actions at all\n2026-09-05 · D89 · Rendimiento stays drawn and deferred; the brief records that its declared blocker is not real\n2026-09-05 · #586 · the Semáforo block is deleted from both Análisis artboards — the engine is retired, not pending\n2026-09-05 · #586 · AssetRow drops its Estado chip and confluence dots (CKP-5 declined with a reason); kit goes to 1.0.0 by its own removal rule\n2026-09-05 · #586 · the detail's block order is stated in the brief instead of implied\n2026-09-05 · D80 · the Semáforo block adopts the code's own copy: the 'Tres señales, leídas por separado' subtitle, and light 1 and 3 bodies read what market/_confluence renders rather than a live-looking reading it does not compute\n2026-09-05 · D79 · Señales BUILT at /signals; the artboard's 'Desde tu última visita' subtitle replaced by the window it actually reads — users carry no last-visit column\n2026-09-05 · D79 · the header here is a TopBarDetail with two parts switched off; the code uses HeaderBar (kit 0.9.0) and this file vendors 0.8.1 — a version lag, not a divergence\n2026-09-05 · D78 · Análisis draws Noticias, Razón P/U histórica and Acerca de la empresa — three sections the code ships and this flow had not drawn\n2026-09-05 · C-4 · MasAnalisis deleted from both Análisis artboards: its volume line is the input D3 gave confluence light 2, and its DISPARADORES are threshold copy ADR-014 does not allow\n2026-09-05 · brief §5 corrected — seven market partials are hardcoded es-MX; it claimed nothing on the band was\n2026-09-05 · brief §6/§7 — D3 is resolved; the gate moved from no-definition to no-engine\n2026-09-05 · Asset · Análisis · Desktop grows 1400 → 1680 to hold the three new cards\n2026-08-29 · reflowed band 0 onto the declared grid: every gutter is 100 now, a 590px hole between Tranquilo and Análisis is gone, and Señales moved from x3700 y−780 — the components zone — into the band in reading order. Desktop stack shifted to respect grid-row-gap (3148 → 3244)\n2026-08-29 · brief rewritten into the eight fixed sections. The prose it replaces carried the why and the dates inline; those live in DECISIONS and here now, and the brief cites numbers\n2026-08-29 · Panorama + Panorama · Desktop: the Radar draws a watchlist row at last. Its own subtitle has read 'De tu cartera y watchlist' all along while every row was a holding, so the artboard was incomplete rather than in conflict with the code. Drawn as an AssetRow instance per D72 — the ISO prefix (USD 248.50) is what tells it from a position, since a holding's value drops the symbol under D10. Desktop grew 860 → 963 and the two artboards below it moved down 103 · X12\n2026-08-29 · Panorama: the Radar's ten AssetRow instances (5 mobile, 5 desktop) now lead with the change and demote the value. AssetRow stays generic — the component defines emphasis positions, not what goes in them, so no kit change and no second component · D69, D72, X12\n2026-08-29 · kit 0.8.1 · Asset · Análisis: the 52-week range moved OUT of Señales to sit under the price as Rango52. Señales is #306-blocked and that row is the one part of it buildable today, so it no longer waits on the rest · CKP-9, #426. Applied to the Desktop artboard in the same pass\n2026-08-29 · kit 0.8.1 · Asset · Análisis: VsPlan's second row now reads the alert threshold instead of a Meta — no target_price will exist · D67, CKP-8. Applied to the Desktop artboard in the same pass\n2026-08-29 · declared grid-x0/brief-w/gutter/y0/row-gap and opened this Log; the file predated both conventions\n2026-08-29 · brief corrected: kit-version-source said 0.8.0 against the file's 0.8.1, and the detail height moved 3037 → 2984 (the hoist freed more than Rango52 added)",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
